00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:01.510 align:start position:0%
 
welcome back time for sport night  history sahel thank you very much well  we start with some breaking news out of  japan  where organizers of the tokyo olympics  have just confirmed that overseas fans  will not be allowed to attend it doesn't  come as a surprise as several reports in  recent weeks suggested the japanese  government  had already made up its mind the main  reason for blocking foreign supporters  is to reduce the risk of spreading  coronavirus  the games have already been delayed by  one year because  of the pandemic well let's bring in  british olympian le taylor mohammed  in manchester who will be competing in  taekwondo at the tokyo games  lotelo overseas fans won't be able to  come and watch you compete  how does that make you feel well  i think it was probably to be expected  we've had such  an unusual year um with you know the  kobe  pandemic that i guess it kind of makes  sense  but it definitely will be different for  me one of the biggest things about the  olympics is having that  uh support uh you know flying from home  obviously family and friends  so an olympics without that is going to  be weird but let's face it it's been a  very weird year  it really has and what about the  japanese fans i know that  uh you you were telling me earlier that  you're expecting a specific atmosphere  when you get there from them  yes i mean the japanese fans are  notorious for being  very quiet and very polite it's um  like small influxes of excitement then  it goes very quiet again  so i'm very fortunate to have competed  in japan before  so i'll be used to it but i think it's  going to be  a bit of a a culture shock for  many olympians who have been at previous  sports events  um it's going to be a bit different  however  um it is what it is i'm just very happy  and grateful that the olympics is  happening  and uh why not why not uh  different doesn't always mean bad it  certainly doesn't well there's been a  lot of talk about the athletes  being vaccinated before they get to  tokyo what's your own situation will you  be vaccinated and has  team gb said anything to you about  vaccinating  the team i would not be getting  vaccinated the  message i have received from team gb is  that there will be no mandatory vaccine  um i'm of the mindset that is not  necessary  i have full confidence in the japanese  organizing committee  the ioc and team gb to uh  make this the safest cleanest  um environment that has ever been for an  olympics  in history with the global pandemic  situation  i think we can all expect that so i  don't think  uh the vaccine uh will be made mandatory  for the athletes because i think  the japanese organizing committee is  gonna do everything they can  we've just seen what uh what they're  doing with the foreign fans not being  allowed to  uh come in they're gonna do everything  they can to make sure it's safe  for all the athletes we spoke to you at  the end of last year about  training in this pandemic you've been  quite lucky you've been able to train  but some athletes haven't been able to  train they haven't had the access to  facilities so  are you concerned about the tokyo  olympics being a level playing field  i think it's going to be a real concern  we are right now  currently seeing a third wave going  across europe  i believe paris and some areas of france  are going to be shut down for  one month um i know italy is  uh now going back into a lockdown or  maybe in a lockdown already  so that's gonna affect many athletes  across the globe not just in europe i  know um  toronto and uh some parts of canada um  so these are big nations who we normally  expect to win  big medals at the olympics my heart goes  out  to those athletes who uh their training  schedule  which has already been massively  affected  um is going to be uh  even more affected um we are very  fortunate at gb  taekwondo where we've been allowed to  train due to our elite athlete exemption  uh it's been very organized and very  grateful for that but across the world  i know that is not the case for  everybody plenty of quarantine  and uh lack of access to facilities  another thing that nobody is really  mentioning is the qualification  situation  half of the athletes have still not been  able to qualify  due to the cobit pandemic so that's  massive in itself i believe the boxing  qualification um the tournament got  halfway through  half the athletes qualified then they  had to cancel the tournament last year  so  there's half of the boxes still waiting  to know  what's going on and that's not just  boxing that's across all the sports so  there's a lot of uh things that clear up  in this four months before  we get to tokyo and just very briefly  you've got four months now to prepare  how are you feeling are you feeling  gold medal fit i'm feeling  very very fit um yes uh bronze in  london uh silva in rio and i'll let you  finish  or the only medal i'm chasing in tokyo  is that gold medal  um it's been difficult uh it's been hard  to focus  uh to maintain focus but thankfully i've  got a wonderful team around me  gary hall's a tremendous leader great  coaches great athletes  and we've all helped each other to get  to this point so i'm feeling  gold medal fits and i can't wait for the  opportunity to get back  on that podium and on top this time  because i want to be number one  well you sound so positive and we wish  you all the best in tokyo  la taylor mohammed thank you very much  for speaking to us  thank you very much for having me and  i'm always positive

